The user's text seems to be a description of matrix multiplication with some typos. The correct description is:

The (i,j)-th entry of the matrix product AB (where A is an m x n matrix and B is an n x p matrix) is given by:

(AB)_{i,j} = \sum_{k=1}^n A_{i,k} B_{k,j}

This is the inner product of the i-th row of A with the j-th column of B.

The space of all m x n matrices with real entries is denoted by \mathbb{R}^{m \times n}.

